title: Beginning
---
<<declare $goodend = 0>>
<<declare $badend = 0>>
<<playMusic frisscityCalm>>
//This needs to be updated with the correct location
<<camera Understory>>
<<fadeIn 2>>
<<place Luna_Neutral>>
<<expression Luna_Neutral arms_neutral>>
Luna: Come on, you stupid SL0P app. Show me the big offers!
<<expression Luna_Neutral annoyed>>
Luna: (Kaya is gonna kill me if I skip out on rent again. Just one big delivery gig should help me break even…)
<<playSFX notification>>
<<expression Luna_Neutral surprised>>
<<show_notification 0>>
Luna: (Huh? It’s a new customer rating on the SL0P app. I better tap it and check it out…)
<<jump BR>>
===

title: BR
---
////////// We need to remove the asset of Luna leaning on her motorbike before we slide in Luna’s character sprite from the left.
<<place Luna_Neutral>>
<<expression Luna_Neutral annoyed>>
Luna: You've got to be joking.
Luna: (I have an option to respond…)
-> Don't respond and close the app
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    Luna: Ugh, whatever.
    <i>I close the app because these people aren’t worth my time.</i>
    <i>Frisscity is home to the ultra-rich who eat up trends, get hooked up with the latest AGENTS tech stack, and want to discover the next worst thing for society.</i>
    //////////<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna shyAnnnoyed>>
    <i>They're fake freaks. And they don't tip.</i>
    <i>I don't wanna deal with them any more than I have to. Frisscity's just where I work. I can't wait for this day to be over so I can get back to my real life in Root Town.</i>
    <<jump CyberdeckT>>
-> Give the reviewer a 1-star rating
    ///////<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaHappy>>
    Luna: Heh, shove it.
    <i>I give Karen a 1-star rating right back, noting how her fruitarian and vegan preferences were never mentioned in the app.</i>
    ////////<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutral>>
    <i>I'm waiting for the day everyone in Frisscity finally decides to upload their brains to the cloud. If the AGENTS founder does it, I'm sure they’ll do it.</i> 
    <i>But me? I’d never fall for a capitalist trick like that.</i>
    <i>Me and Root Town refuse to integrate with AGENTS technology. Life outside of AGENTS and Frisscity is hard, but it's real. And it's home.</i>
    <<jump CyberdeckT>>
-> Doxx their address on an online forum for SL0P drivers
    <<set $badend += 1>>
    <i>Instead of leaving them a review, I do much worse. I post their address on a public online forum and warn fellow drivers from Root Town not to take delivery orders from them.</i>
    ///////<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaHappyArms>>
    Luna: Now all of SL0P will know what you have done. Good luck getting your stupid apples and cheese.
    ////////<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
    <i>This is the shit I put up with in Frisscity. I break my back for baecoins for people who chase trends and chase surgeries to get hooked up with the latest AGENTS technology.</i>
    <i>But me? I refuse to be augmented.</i>
    <i>I wish Frisscity would just disappear.</i>
    <<jump CyberdeckT>>
===

title: CyberdeckT
---
<<playSFX notification>>
//Luna with lunaAnnoyedArms
<<show_notification 1>>
Luna: Now what?
//<<fadeIn 2>>
<<set_cyberdeck_state 1>>
<<jump Tutorial_Chat>>
===

title: Tutorial_Chat
---
<<wait 0.5>>

Nat: Hey-yo! How’s your night going?
Luna: like slop. as usual. 
Nat: Ooo, bummer. Well I wanted to ask how you’re liking the cyberdeck I made ya?
Luna: i’m typing rn, aren’t i?
Nat: I know! But have you used any of the other features?
Luna: …
Nat: How about I show you around the NATIO 3000?
Nat: Get it? 
Nat: The NAT-io? 
Luna: cute…
Nat: You’re currently on the message screen! Click on the tabs to sort through all the messages you get. Like spam, news, and super-important messages from me ;)
Nat: Your settings are also in the cyberdeck in case you wanna fine-tune things like sound volume or message speed!
Nat: You can also quit the game using the Settings tab on your cyberdeck.
Nat: I also programmed a super cute mini game just for you! Play it whenever you want. 
Nat: Lemme know when you get a new high score, k~?
Nat: The History button also lets you peep at previous conversations you had with others. (Or yourself.) 
Nat: And when you’re done tinkering around, just press the Exit button! You can return to the cyberdeck by clicking on the NATIO 3000 logo in the game.
Nat: Did that make sense? 
Luna: yeah, thx. can i go back to work now?
Nat: Of course! Just let me know if you need anything
<<wait_for_cyberdeck_exit>>
<<enable_cyberdeck_exit>>
//<<loadScene JenScene>>
===
